[{:db/id 17592186152200 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-19ad1761-3136-5be8-b038-5aa62265f48b" "question-1c04d4c5-9913-59ea-a83f-46d8bb7c02cf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-19ad1761-3136-5be8-b038-5aa62265f48b" :question/id #uuid "19ad1761-3136-5be8-b038-5aa62265f48b" :question/math-academy-id "q-80526" :question/problem "![](images/88/8866056ce5c7c80ed8452246cc3a40074b6841615ed6ef472e7a1612709e51fa.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${∬}_{R}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,1]\\times [-3,2]$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [-3,3]$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [-2,2]$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement II is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement III is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e2a9dd81-ee99-5b34-b7e2-398216f26e54"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e2a9dd81-ee99-5b34-b7e2-398216f26e54" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2a9dd81-ee99-5b34-b7e2-398216f26e54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-5f3e8aa2-20ed-5607-9c37-0e3dceaf9028" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4a78a72b-b4d7-5293-8aba-7c35212132ae" "answer-f078a363-807c-53b3-b111-d4c6e7e91d19" "answer-9f70c45e-aafb-568b-ad0e-18cd0c73be10" "answer-5f3e8aa2-20ed-5607-9c37-0e3dceaf9028" "answer-30dc624a-6195-52a9-9917-f3684e4a574f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a78a72b-b4d7-5293-8aba-7c35212132ae" :answer/id #uuid "4a78a72b-b4d7-5293-8aba-7c35212132ae" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f078a363-807c-53b3-b111-d4c6e7e91d19" :answer/id #uuid "f078a363-807c-53b3-b111-d4c6e7e91d19" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f70c45e-aafb-568b-ad0e-18cd0c73be10" :answer/id #uuid "9f70c45e-aafb-568b-ad0e-18cd0c73be10" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f3e8aa2-20ed-5607-9c37-0e3dceaf9028" :answer/id #uuid "5f3e8aa2-20ed-5607-9c37-0e3dceaf9028" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-30dc624a-6195-52a9-9917-f3684e4a574f" :answer/id #uuid "30dc624a-6195-52a9-9917-f3684e4a574f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152198 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1654ded7-c0bc-579c-a9e9-6daa6a1243e7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1654ded7-c0bc-579c-a9e9-6daa6a1243e7" :question/id #uuid "1654ded7-c0bc-579c-a9e9-6daa6a1243e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-86894" :question/problem "![](images/5d/5d8f57afa16e99c13e6e36c5544a7c7594da13321bd3d01692a5a296a20953d7.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-2,2]\\times [-2,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\{\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D∖R\\end{aligned}$\n\nII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$\n\nIII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ x{e}^{y}, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D$ and the rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/ce/ce9b9f3435a94b3f9f87b195e5b1591c80281b23cfb76ceb8e79cdeec3ae66b0.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal $x{e}^{y}$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}x{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- We cannot use functions I and II. Both of these functions are not identically zero for all points in $R\\,∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(2,2)\\in R\\,∖\\,D,$ but the functions are nonzero at this point.\n\n- Function III equals $x{e}^{y}$ on $D$ and equals $0$ outside $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-30306495-7925-535a-81a1-49a15747abcb"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-30306495-7925-535a-81a1-49a15747abcb" :answer-field/id #uuid "30306495-7925-535a-81a1-49a15747abcb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-6e995b4f-80df-5a44-ac52-ef3e8528fb3d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c738fcf4-81ab-523b-a4a3-3c52b0e51091" "answer-7ea449c7-e858-51b4-bdf2-6beadec281c8" "answer-e52b4a76-97bf-58a6-8111-6703e511f2da" "answer-fdb50184-5f7d-5a30-8c1d-9227e10a07fa" "answer-6e995b4f-80df-5a44-ac52-ef3e8528fb3d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c738fcf4-81ab-523b-a4a3-3c52b0e51091" :answer/id #uuid "c738fcf4-81ab-523b-a4a3-3c52b0e51091" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ea449c7-e858-51b4-bdf2-6beadec281c8" :answer/id #uuid "7ea449c7-e858-51b4-bdf2-6beadec281c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e52b4a76-97bf-58a6-8111-6703e511f2da" :answer/id #uuid "e52b4a76-97bf-58a6-8111-6703e511f2da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fdb50184-5f7d-5a30-8c1d-9227e10a07fa" :answer/id #uuid "fdb50184-5f7d-5a30-8c1d-9227e10a07fa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e995b4f-80df-5a44-ac52-ef3e8528fb3d" :answer/id #uuid "6e995b4f-80df-5a44-ac52-ef3e8528fb3d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186354532 :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curves $y={x}^{2}-1$ and $y=|x|.$ If $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+1}, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin D\\end{aligned}$\n\nII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+1}, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$\n\nIII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}+1}, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186354533 :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed by the curves $y=-|x|+2$ and $y=|x|.$ If $R=[-1,1]\\times [0,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({x}^{5}-{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}-{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin D\\end{aligned}$\n\nII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}-{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$\n\nIII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{5}-{y}^{2}, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-1c04d4c5-9913-59ea-a83f-46d8bb7c02cf" :question/id #uuid "1c04d4c5-9913-59ea-a83f-46d8bb7c02cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-129893" :question/problem "Let $D$ be a finite region enclosed between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}+2$ and the $x$-axis. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+3y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,3]$\n\nII. ${∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-2,2]\\times [0,2]$\n\nIII. ${∬}_{R}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\\,$ where $R=[-3,3]\\times [-4,4]$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's draw our region $D:$\n\n![](images/3b/3bfc135232008824ae0522bcc8454c5f97c2dfd13fb6e333e146a040ccbc1f22.png)\n\nNotice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+3y), & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+3y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statements I is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Statements II is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement III is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3b56bb6c-74dd-5bd4-a9cd-cbed30098ff9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3b56bb6c-74dd-5bd4-a9cd-cbed30098ff9" :answer-field/id #uuid "3b56bb6c-74dd-5bd4-a9cd-cbed30098ff9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-daf363de-8d3